<div class="row">
  <div class="large-6 large-centered columns">
    <div class="banner-text">
      <h1 class="banner-text__title">
      $<%= number_to_currency(@totalLosses, precision: 0, unit: '') %>
      </h1>
      <h2 class="banner-text__subtitle">lost to HB2</h2>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="row">
  <div class="small-12 columns">
    <p class="lead">On March 23rd, 2016, the state of North Carolina signed <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Public_Facilities_Privacy_%26_Security_Act#North_Carolina_House_Bill_2" class="link" target="_blank">HB2</a> into law. We've been <a href="https://www.americanprogress.org/issues/lgbt/news/2016/04/13/135391/north-carolinas-discriminatory-h-b-2-threatens-more-than-half-billion-dollars-in-economic-activity/" class="link" target="_blank">losing money</a> ever since. The question is: how long are we going to let this continue?</p>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="row">
  <div class="small-12 columns">
    <%= render partial: 'partials/losses', locals: { losses: @allLosses } %>
    <%= render partial: 'partials/linkToAll' %>
  </div>
</div>
